\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Proposition}
\title{Independence of the inversion eigenpairs}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{At each self-opposite label in the \vocabk{inversion product}{fdip-01AV}, the negative part has an orthonormal basis of antiunitary pairs whose two members share an inversion sign. Multiplying one sign from each such pair gives the inversion product independently of all choices of simultaneous eigenpairs.}

\proof{\p{The two inversion eigenspaces are orthogonal since a unitary involution is self-adjoint. Each intersected with the negative spectral subspace is stable under #{A}: its inversion eigenvalue is real and #{A} commutes with both operators. The induction in \ref{fdip-01AO} supplies an orthonormal pair basis in each intersection. The number of pairs of inversion sign #{-1} is half the negative-inversion intersection dimension. Multiplying their signs gives the definition, while the other pairs have sign #{+1}.}}
